<title>USA: Vivus impotence suppository gets FDA okay.</title>
<headline>Vivus impotence suppository gets FDA okay.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vivus Inc said Wednesday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has cleared its impotence suppository treatment for marketing.  </p>
<p>The company said it expects shipping the urethral suppository, called MUSE, in early 1997.</p>
<p>Vivus said about 30 percent of men between the ages of 40 and 70 in the United States suffer from moderate to complete erectile dysfunction. It said the potential world market is estimated at 47 million men by the year 2000.</p>
<p>Vivus, founded in 1991, is developing various treatments for erectile dysfunction.</p>
<p>Vivus shares were 34-3/4 at Tuesday's close.</p>
